# Breadcrumbs

The last crumb is the current page. It uses the brand color. Earlier crumbs stay muted and stay links.

## Current page

- The last item has `class="is-current"` and `aria-current="page"`.
- Its color is `var(--primary)` from the one rule in `src/styles.css`. Do not set another color on that item in a route.
- Ancestors are links in `var(--muted)`. Hover may use `var(--primary)` or `var(--primary-dark)`.
- Separators stay `var(--muted)` or `var(--line)`. They are not the current page.
- `is-current` without `aria-current="page"` is not a breadcrumb. The claim-link state uses that class for a different color.
- Below 768px the trail is 12px with a 6px gap. That size lives once in `src/styles.css`. Do not repeat it in a route. Desktop stays at the route size, 13px or 14px.
- A public trainer page is the exception on that phone size: 11px, body weight, a 4px gap, and 8px under the trail. The city phrase and the name would otherwise wrap into a heavy second line. The crumbs stay.
- On a trainer page the city crumb is the city name (`Минск`), and the `BreadcrumbList` name is that same word. The city page title stays `Тренеры в Минске`.

## Example

```tsx
<nav aria-label="Хлебные крошки">
  <Link to="/">Главная</Link>
  <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <span className="is-current" aria-current="page">{name}</span>
</nav>
```

```css
/* wrong: the current page turns dark or gray */
.crumbs .is-current { color: var(--dark); }

/* right: leave the color to styles.css */
```
